Conducted comprehensive analysis of Aerofit treadmill dataset using Python, NumPy, Pandas, Matplotlib, and Seaborn to identify customer profiles and purchasing patterns for three product models(KP281, KP481, KP781).
Utilized various data visualization techniques to uncover trends and present findings effectively.
Conducted EDA, identifying patterns, outliers and missing values in the dataset. Developed data-driven customer profiling approach, enabling tailored product offerings and promotional campaigns.
Identified key customer segments for each model:
KP781 (premium): Incomes over $70,000, education 18+ years, run 220+ miles- facilitating a potential 25% increase in high-end product sales
KP281: Women, incomes below $70,000, aged 40+, 2-4 days/week usage- leading to a potential 18% boost in KP281 sales
KP481: Women aged 32-37 or younger individuals under 25, incomes $50,000-$70,000, active lifestyles- contributing to a  potential 12% increase in sales within these customer segments
Recommended introducing financing options and value-added services to expand customer base by potential 15%.
Suggested loyalty programs and community-building initiatives to improve customer retention by potential 12%.
